@startuml FIG-CL-TAV-08
skinparam shadowing false
title FIG-CL-TAV-08 Parametric\nSysML 1.6 notation-based views; executable/metamodel conformance is not claimed\nconstraints shown, not claimed solved

class I_allow <<constraint>> {
  I : allowed timing interval
}
class eps <<constraint>> {
  epsilon : measurement error bound
}
class J_meas <<constraint>> {
  J : feasible interval from measurement
}
class cmin_b <<constraint>> {
  cmin > 0
  cost(t) >= cmin
  cost(ERROR) >= cmin
}
class budget <<constraint>> {
  B finite XOR Kmax finite
}
class score <<constraint>> {
  s(t) = worst remaining |Hk|
  over Obs(t,qk)
}
class update <<constraint>> {
  Hk+1 = {h in Hk | O(h,t,qk) intersects Izk}
}

I_allow .. J_meas
eps .. J_meas
J_meas .. update
cmin_b .. budget
score .. update
budget .. score

note bottom
  Positive-but-vanishing costs are not a termination proof.
  ERROR is under the same chosen constraint as ordinary tests.
  Parametric view displays constraints; it does not claim they are solved.
  Selected mode is BUDGET XOR ROUNDS.
end note
@enduml
